# Environment variables consumed by Stromy Deliverables.
#
# Every ${VAR} referenced in .agents/mcp.json must appear here so the
# plugin-completeness validator passes (Inv #4) and downstream clients
# know which secrets they need to set.
#
# Copy to .env (never commit .env) and fill in real values.

# Apify API token (BYOK) — authorizes the official Apify MCP (research-apify
# skill). Create at https://console.apify.com/account/integrations and set a
# console spend cap (Settings → Limits → Maximum monthly usage). Billed to your
# own Apify account; never transits Stromy infra. This is the org's one Apify
# token var (also used by lead-scout); .agents/mcp.json maps it into the
# subprocess as APIFY_TOKEN (the name the official MCP reads).
APIFY_API_TOKEN=
#
# Codex only: render-mcp.py strips ${VAR} env refs for Codex, so under Codex the
# Apify subprocess inherits the shell env — also export APIFY_TOKEN (same value)
# there. Claude/Gemini/VS Code get the mapping above and need only APIFY_API_TOKEN.
